"""SWD header: bare through-hole pads at 1.27 mm pitch for an ST-Link's SWD lines, and optionally
its supply and reset pins.

Default: three pads, 1 GND, 2 SWDIO, 3 SWCLK: the middle three contacts of the v1 main board's SWD
connector P1 (MicrasPCB e34fb9a, boards/main: 1 SWD_VDD, 2 GND, 3 SWDIO, 4 SWCLK, 5 NRST) in the
same order, without NRST.
With `supply`: four pads in the 4-pin order of a clone ST-Link's 1.27 mm SWD lead (owner,
2026-11-01): 1 SWDIO, 2 GND, 3 SWCLK, 4 VDD, VDD taking the probe's 5 V pin into the board (the
board decides what that pin feeds; the main board takes it through a Schottky diode into its regulators'
input). The lead plugs on pin 1 to pad 1; turned round, or shifted one pad either way, the probe's
5 V never lands on the board's GND.
With `supply` and `reset`: five pads, the reset line first and then the lead's four: 1 NRST,
2 SWDIO, 3 GND, 4 SWCLK, 5 VDD (owner, 2026-11-03): the 4-pin lead plugs on pads 2-5 and the
probe's RST wire on pad 1. The variants number their pads differently: a board switching
variants re-routes the header.

Misplugs of the four-pin lead on the five-pad variant (lead contacts SWDIO, GND, SWCLK, 5 V):
- on pads 1-4 (one pad toward pad 1): 5 V on SWCLK (pad 4), the probe's ground on SWDIO;
- on pads 3-6 (one pad off the far end): 5 V on no pad, the probe's SWCLK on VDD and SWDIO on GND;
- turned round on pads 2-5: 5 V on SWDIO (pad 2), the probe's ground on SWCLK;
- turned round on pads 1-4: 5 V on NRST (pad 1), the grounds together;
- turned round on pads 3-6: 5 V on GND (pad 3), the probe's ground on VDD.
What each case does depends on the board's nets; the board's docstring says.

Footprints: KiCad's PinHeader_1x03_P1.27mm_Vertical, PinHeader_1x04_P1.27mm_Vertical and
PinHeader_1x05_P1.27mm_Vertical (kicad-footprint-generator, connector/pin_header_socket) with their
1.0 mm pads grown to 1.05 mm and their 0.12 mm silkscreen lines to 0.15 mm (JLCPCB's minimum),
square pad 1 with the silkscreen's pin-1 corner beside it, on 0.65 mm drills at 1.27 mm pitch: a
0.2 mm ring against JLCPCB's 0.18 mm PTH minimum and 0.22 mm between pads (rules/jlcpcb.kicad_dru).
The pads are numbered along the row; the symbols map the signals onto them. No part is placed: a
1.27 mm pitch header (or the probe's wires) is soldered by hand, so the header is excluded from the
BOM and the placement file. Each footprint embeds KiCad's model of its header all the same, so the
layout's height checks see the soldered header.
"""

prefix = config(str, default="J", help="Reference designator prefix")
supply = config(bool, default=False, help="four pads in a clone ST-Link's order, 1 SWDIO, 2 GND, 3 SWCLK, 4 VDD")
reset = config(bool, default=False, help="with supply: five pads, 1 NRST, 2 SWDIO, 3 GND, 4 SWCLK, 5 VDD")

GND = io(Ground)
SWDIO = io(Net)
SWCLK = io(Net)
VDD = io(Power, optional=True, help="pad 4 (pad 5 with reset), with supply = True: the probe's supply pin")
NRST = io(Net, optional=True, help="pad 1, with reset = True: the target's reset line")

if reset and not supply:
    error("SwdHeader: reset = True needs supply = True (the five-pad variant)")

pins = {"GND": GND, "SWDIO": SWDIO, "SWCLK": SWCLK}
if supply:
    pins["VDD"] = VDD
if reset:
    pins["NRST"] = NRST

Component(
    name="J",
    prefix=prefix,
    symbol=Symbol(
        library="SwdHeader.kicad_sym",
        name="SwdHeader5" if reset else ("SwdHeader4" if supply else "SwdHeader"),
    ),
    pins=pins,
    skip_bom=True,
    skip_pos=True,
)
